Dear Dr. Meeker,
	Thanks for your advice this morning, I figured out the
problem. Pointers of course. It seems Splus passes arrays as one
long vector. I was using a double index so of course the array was
out of bounds. Is there a way to force Splus to send a two
dimensional array or is everything stored as vectors? Anyway the new
commands for an alpha are for future reference

1) compiling:
 Splus SHLIB -o <out filename>.so <src1>.c <src2>.c ..... -lm
returns a compiled libray <name>.so

2) loading: the command is now
dyn.load.shared("./<out filename>.so")

3)calling: Calling the C or fortran routine is the same as in
earlier versions using the .C or .Fortran commands

